@startuml
title 3.6.16 List escalated claims
caption UC-112 | Planned | Proposed design
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
show footbox
<style>
lifeLine {
    LineStyle 0
}
</style>
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor white
    ActorBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBorderColor black
    GroupBackgroundColor white
    GroupHeaderBackgroundColor white
}

' Source: docs/requirements/uc.md
' Main entity migration: apps/api-node/src/migrations/002_lost_found_schema.sql
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Staff / Admin" as Actor
participant "Proposed Escalated Cases" as Page
participant "Proposed Claims API" as API
participant "Proposed Support Case Service" as Service
participant "claims" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open List escalated claims
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: Search escalated cases (proposed interface)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: List escalated claims
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Require Staff/Admin and case-scoped access policy
Service -> Table: 6: Proposed: SELECT escalated claims by state, age and handler
activate Table
Table --> Service: 7: Paginated case summaries
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 8: Redact private conversation and evidence until explicitly\nauthorized
Service --> API: 9: Escalated case list
API --> Page: 10: HTTP 200: Escalated case list
Page --> Actor: 11: Show authorized result
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: Proposed rejection: invalid input / authorization
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: Planned: custody queue is a different goal. General escalation/handler schema and endpoint
are not implemented.
endlegend
@enduml
